Third-party runtime dependencies

Luxafor Monitor has no third-party runtime dependencies. All functionality
is implemented directly on top of Apple system frameworks (IOKit,
AVFoundation, Accessibility/ApplicationServices, SwiftUI) that ship with
macOS. This is a deliberate supply-chain minimization choice; see
CONTRIBUTING.md before proposing a new dependency.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Luxafor USB HID protocol

The `LuxaforKit` module implements the Luxafor device's USB HID control
protocol (vendor ID, report byte layout, and command opcodes) as a
clean-room implementation derived from publicly documented protocol
information. No source code, headers, or binaries from Luxafor's own SDKs
or drivers were copied, decompiled, or otherwise incorporated.

The USB vendor ID (0x04D8, Microchip Technology Inc.), the Luxafor Flag's
product ID (0xF372), and the "set static color" HID output report layout
were cross-checked across multiple independent public sources describing
the Luxafor protocol, including pyluxa4's published USB API documentation,
the MarcMeszaros/luxafor-go project, fmartingr/pyluxafor's udev rules, and
JnyJny/busylight's device table. Support for other Luxafor models
(Mini/Multi/Orb/Mute) is based on secondary references that were not
independently verified against real hardware; see
Sources/LuxaforKit/LuxaforProtocol.swift for details.

